endedSize\":{\"height\":\"40px\"}},\"requiredServices\":{\"names\":[],\"status\":\"not-required\",\"missing\":[]},\"optionalServices\":{\"names\":[\"agent-ui.locale\"],\"available\":[\"agent-ui.locale\"]},\"childSlots\":{}},{\"pluginId\":\"theme-provider\",\"componentPresentation\":{\"packageVersion\":\"0.0.1\",\"module\":\"@za38.03/agent-ui-plugins/theme-provider\",\"component\":\"ThemeProviderPlugin\",\"facts\":{\"presentation\":\"The built-in theme keys are light, dark and violet; the default is violet. A custom brand color such as blue is a project CSS palette customization, not a new theme enum value. ThemeProviderPlugin renders its children and does not accept palette/color props.\",\"composition\":\"Keep the existing theme service and AgentUIRoot. Agent theme props or createAgentUIThemeService(initialTheme) select a built-in preset; AppUIModel does not configure component props. Do not add another theme Runtime or edit npm implementation files.\",\"styles\":\"Import @za38.03/agent-ui-plugins/styles.css before project overrides. Scoped palette selectors are :is(.agent-ui-root, .agent-ui-conversation)[data-theme=\\\"violet\\\"] for the default preset. Override --agent-brand and --agent-brand-solid for the brand and solid actions; --primary, --ring, --sidebar-primary and --sidebar-ring are semantic control/sidebar colors. Violet derives --primary and sidebar/focus colors from --agent-brand-solid; neutral light/dark derive --agent-brand from --primary, so override both when customizing those presets. Other public tokens include --background, --foreground, --card, --muted, --border, --input, --primary-foreground, --sidebar and --sidebar-foreground. Keep surfaces/readability coherent and verify rendered colors and theme switching. These names describe this installed package; project CSS overrides need no source takeover.\"}},\"name\":\"Headless Theme Service Provider\",\"description\":\"Provides the shared Agent UI theme preset service to other UI plugins.\",\"capa